---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards & Rating Methodology — QuoteShield"
  description="Discover QuoteShield's editorial standards, data verification process, fact-checking protocols, and carrier rating formula."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="badge badge-trust">Editorial Excellence</span>
      <h1>Our Editorial Standards & Methodology</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">How our team of licensed insurance professionals researches, calculates, and fact-checks every rate guide.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container page-content article-content">
    <p>
      At <strong>QuoteShield</strong>, we hold our content to the highest standards of accuracy, objectivity, and consumer utility. Insurance policies represent critical financial safety nets for American families. Misleading advice or outdated rate tables can result in catastrophic underinsurance or costly overpayment.
    </p>

    <h2>1. The Four Pillars of Our Editorial Process</h2>

    <div class="card" style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      <h3>1. Primary Source Data Collection</h3>
      <p>
        We do not rely on second-hand aggregator figures or generic quotes. Our data research team pulls regulatory filings directly from state insurance department databases, the NAIC System for Electronic Rates & Forms Filing (SERFF), and audited annual financial statements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      <h3>2. Professional Credentialed Review</h3>
      <p>
        Every piece of content—including rate comparison guides, policy breakdown analyses, and calculator algorithms—is drafted or reviewed by a subject matter expert holding professional designations such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>CPCU</strong> (Chartered Property Casualty Underwriter) — for auto, homeowners, and liability;</li>
        <li><strong>CFP®</strong> (Certified Financial Planner) — for life insurance and estate planning;</li>
        <li><strong>CLU</strong> (Chartered Life Underwriter) — for health and life insurance structures.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      <h3>3. Annual & Quarterly Rate Recalibration</h3>
      <p>
        Because insurance carriers file revised rate revisions throughout the fiscal year to account for loss-cost inflation, parts availability, and catastrophe modeling, QuoteShield audits rate tables quarterly to ensure consumer figures remain relevant.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      <h3>4. Rigorous Fact-Checking and Corrections Policy</h3>
      <p>
        If an insurer introduces a new endorsement, modifies state availability, or files updated rate tariffs, we issue public revisions promptly. We invite consumers and carriers to report discrepancies via our <a href="/contact/">editorial correction portal</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>2. Carrier Star Rating Formula</h2>
    <p>
      Our proprietary carrier rating model evaluates insurers across 18 distinct data points grouped into five weighted criteria:
    </p>

    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Evaluation Category</th>
            <th>Weight</th>
            <th>Primary Benchmark Sources</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Financial Solvency</strong></td>
            <td>25%</td>
            <td>AM Best Financial Strength Ratings (A++ to B-), S&P Global, Fitch</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Claims Handling & Satisfaction</strong></td>
            <td>25%</td>
            <td>NAIC Complaint Index, J.D. Power U.S. Auto & Property Claims Studies</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Coverage & Policy Flexibility</strong></td>
            <td>20%</td>
            <td>Endorsements, gap insurance, accident forgiveness, OEM repair coverage</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Pricing Competitiveness</strong></td>
            <td>20%</td>
            <td>State rate filing averages across clean, credit-challenged, and young driver profiles</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Digital Experience & Support</strong></td>
            <td>10%</td>
            <td>App Store & Google Play verified user ratings, online claim tracking speed</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>3. Separation of Sales and Editorial</h2>
    <p>
      QuoteShield maintains a strict firewall between editorial decision-making and commercial revenue teams. Insurers cannot pay for inclusion in our guides, purchase higher star ratings, or influence our editorial critique. Our editors write for one stakeholder only: <strong>the American policyholder</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0c1e33 0%, #153252 100%);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: 860px;
  }
</style>
